  "findings": [
    {
      "subject": "START edge and model phase",
      "conclusion": "No definite repeated-START defect found in the inspected path. handle builds physical-source signals and calls begin once for the frame-level startEdge; lastButtons.start is updated before the next frame. Wi-Fi has no startSeq and therefore uses the false-to-true boolean edge. long_press retains true rather than adding another edge. M.start only accepts garage and changes to countdown after rebuilding six bounded physics car objects while preserving prior specs/conditions.",
      "refs": [
        "game.js:95-108",
        "game-model.js:47-58"
      ],
      "limitation": "This is source reasoning, not a traced count of begin calls in the failed APK run."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Scene construction and resource reuse",
      "conclusion": "The UsedCarRenderer constructor is called once at startup. The first garage render already calls setTrack and builds the track world. Unchanged track.id returns without rebuilding. All six car models are prepared by ensureCars in the garage; same modelId:color entries are reused after START because M.start preserves specs. No repeated renderer/world/model creation attributable to START was found.",
      "refs": [
        "game.js:149",
        "renderer-3d.js:91-105",
        "renderer-3d.js:159-169"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "First race render differs from garage",
      "conclusion": "START changes world/garage visibility, car placement/visibility, camera, headlight intensity and vehicle environment map. World GPU rendering/shader/texture work can therefore occur on the first countdown draw even though CPU-side geometry already exists. Existing WebGL render/getError calls are synchronous. First audio unlock may create one AudioContext, three oscillators and a bounded two-second noise buffer.",
      "refs": [
        "renderer-3d.js:166-170",
        "renderer-3d.js:160",
        "vehicle-models.js:66-76",
        "materials.js:135-174",
        "audio.js:4-13"
      ],
      "limitation": "These are actual code-path differences, not evidence that GPU, audio or a particular call caused the AVD failure."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Input and diagnostic snapshots",
      "conclusion": "getInputs consumes the bridge once in initial startup and once per animation frame. begin/resume/garage read cached latest values. The 200ms UI/publish timer does not call getInputs. PureTVQA.snapshot reads controllerAdapter.peek and copied model fields, with no second native input snapshot.",
      "refs": [
        "game.js:63-90",
        "game.js:132-149"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Synchronous loops",
      "conclusion": "The countdown update clamps dt to 0.25 seconds and consumes its accumulator by fixed 1/120 steps, so the first countdown frame has at most 30 rule steps. Track camera nearest uses a finite 640-segment scan. Track building loops and environment map generation are bounded; their track/theme caches were inspected. No definite START-specific unbounded loop was found.",
      "refs": [
        "game-model.js:201-210",
        "tracks.js:50-61",
        "renderer-3d.js:91-105",
        "materials.js:135-174"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Log attribution",
      "conclusion": "The 17:02:29 Chromium renderer 3078 crash message is from parent PID 2689 com.google.android.katniss:search; its renderer allocation is explicitly logged under Katniss. Used Car is PID 4152 and its WebView renderer is 4203. The Katniss event is not evidence of a Used Car app renderer crash. Used Car does log Skipped 88 frames at 17:02:44.772, and tile-memory warnings predate START during menu.",
      "limitation": "No Used Car FATAL EXCEPTION, OutOfMemoryError, WebGL draw failed or Used Car Racing startup failed match was found in this retained continuous log. Missing diagnostics do not establish the absence of an underlying failure."
    }
  ],
